{
  "vcon": "0.4.0",
  "uuid": "1828c940-9723-87c5-bc11-bc7f724ca864",
  "created_at": "2026-01-02T12:06:55-05:00",
  "subject": "Inbound call, Public Works",
  "parties": [
    {
      "name": "Lucille Mancini",
      "role": "resident",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    },
    {
      "name": "Kevin Sousa",
      "role": "clerk",
      "validation": "synthetic"
    }
  ],
  "dialog": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T12:05:02-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Public Works, this is Kevin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T12:05:05-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Hi Kevin, Lucille Mancini. I'm on speaker, I've got my hands full, so tell me if you can't hear me."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T12:05:12-05:00",
      "duration": 4,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sounds fine so far. What can I do for you?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T12:05:16-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There's a pothole on my road that the city filled last week with that cold patch stuff. Well, it's gone. Washed right out. It's a hole again, bigger than before."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T12:05:26-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, so a repair from last week that didn't hold. Which street is it on?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T12:05:32-05:00",
      "duration": 9,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah, I'd rather not give the street over the phone, I just want to ask about the process. Can you log it without that, or no?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T12:05:41-05:00",
      "duration": 12,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "I can note the call, but a crew really needs a location to go out. I'll write it down as a washed-out cold patch, and you can send the street in when you're ready. Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T12:05:53-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Yeah. If somebody hits that hole and wrecks a tire or a rim, does the city reimburse for car damage?"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T12:06:00-05:00",
      "duration": 14,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "There's a claim process for that. You'd file a claim with the city, and they look at it case by case. I can't tell you whether one would be paid. Best to keep your repair receipts and take a photo of the hole."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T12:06:14-05:00",
      "duration": 10,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Okay, receipts and a photo. Got it. [pause] Sorry, hang on. The neighbor's dog is going off again. He barks at the mail carrier every morning, like clockwork. Anyway, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T12:06:24-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "No problem. So I've got the washed-out patch noted, and the claim info for you."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T12:06:30-05:00",
      "duration": 6,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Can I get a reference number for this call? So I can say I reported it."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T12:06:36-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "Sure, give me a second. [pause] I'm logging it now. Your reference number is PW, dash, one, zero, four, seven."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T12:06:43-05:00",
      "duration": 3,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "PW, one, zero, four, seven. Okay, thanks Kevin."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T12:06:46-05:00",
      "duration": 7,
      "parties": [
        1
      ],
      "originator": 1,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You're welcome. Call back with the street whenever you're ready, and give them that number. Have a good weekend."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "start": "2026-01-02T12:06:53-05:00",
      "duration": 2,
      "parties": [
        0
      ],
      "originator": 0,
      "mediatype": "text/plain",
      "encoding": "none",
      "body": "You too. Bye."
    }
  ],
